ASTRONOMICAL DATA SOURCES — DERIVED DATA, NOT IMAGE TEXTURES
-------------------------------------------------------------
Star positions, magnitudes and approximate colors in public/data/stars.json
are generated by scripts/build-stars.js from bsc5-short.json in
Bretton Wade's YaleBrightStarCatalog project (MIT License;
Copyright (c) 2016 Bretton Wade). Original catalog: Yale Bright Star
Catalog, fifth edition. The generated file contains converted coordinates
and color estimates, not the original bsc5-short.json file.
Source: https://github.com/brettonw/YaleBrightStarCatalog
License: https://github.com/brettonw/YaleBrightStarCatalog/blob/master/LICENSE

Asteroid elements in public/data/asteroids.bin and metadata in
public/data/asteroids.json are generated by scripts/build-asteroids.js
using NASA/JPL Small-Body Database Query API. This is a source credit,
not a claim that the asteroid data are team-created measurements.
API: https://ssd-api.jpl.nasa.gov/doc/sbdb_query.html

The binary planet/spacecraft positions in public/ephemeris/*.bin,
indexed by public/ephemeris/index.json, are generated by
scripts/generate-horizons-cache.js from NASA/JPL Horizons vectors.
API: https://ssd-api.jpl.nasa.gov/doc/horizons.html
JPL API fair-use policy: https://ssd-api.jpl.nasa.gov/doc/

These derived files retain their source acknowledgments. Neither the
